<section class="service-list">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Core E-Commerce Services</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Every engagement starts with what your store is actually doing today &mdash; the funnel, the catalog,
      the order flow, the reporting &mdash; and works down a list ordered by what it&rsquo;s worth, not by
      what&rsquo;s easiest to build.
    </p>

    <ul class="service-grid">
      <li class="service-card">
        <h3>Conversion &amp; Checkout</h3>
        <p class="service-tagline">Find the leaks before you buy more traffic.</p>
        <p>
          Product page structure, cart behavior, shipping and tax presentation, payment methods, guest
          checkout, and mobile performance. I instrument each step, find where sessions die, and fix the
          ones with real money behind them &mdash; then confirm the change held.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="service-card">
        <h3>Catalog, Product Data &amp; Merchandising</h3>
        <p class="service-tagline">Clean data upstream is why everything downstream works.</p>
        <p>
          Taxonomy, variants, attributes, and imagery that stay coherent as the catalog grows. Search and
          collection tuning, pricing and promotion rules, and feeds to Google, Meta, and marketplaces that
          don&rsquo;t get disapproved the week you launch.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="service-card">
        <h3>Operations &amp; Systems Integration</h3>
        <p class="service-tagline">Fewer spreadsheets between your store and your business.</p>
        <p>
          Order routing, inventory sync, fulfillment and 3PL handoffs, returns, and subscriptions. Wiring
          the store to your ERP, accounting, and support tools so operations stop depending on someone
          remembering to run an export.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="service-card">
        <h3>Platform Strategy &amp; Replatforming</h3>
        <p class="service-tagline">Stay, extend, or move — with the reasoning shown.</p>
        <p>
          An honest read on Shopify, BigCommerce, WooCommerce, custom, or headless for your specific
          catalog and order volume. When a move is right, a migration plan that protects URLs and rankings,
          carries order and customer history, and has a rollback.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="service-card">
        <h3>Analytics, Attribution &amp; Lifecycle</h3>
        <p class="service-tagline">Numbers you can defend in a meeting.</p>
        <p>
          Server-side and client-side tracking that survives a theme or checkout change, revenue reporting
          tied to margin rather than gross sales, and email, SMS, and retention flows judged on repeat
          purchase rate and LTV.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="service-card">
