<section class="process">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How an Engagement Runs</h2>
    <p>
      No discovery phase that bills for a month and ends in a slide deck. The first pass is measurement,
      the second is a prioritized list, and after that the work ships in order.
    </p>

    <ol class="process-steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Measure</strong>
        <span>Walk the funnel, the catalog, and the order flow as they exist today. Establish the baseline numbers everything after this is judged against.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prioritize</strong>
        <span>Rank findings by revenue impact against effort. You see the list, the reasoning, and what I&rsquo;d do first if it were my store.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ship</strong>
        <span>Work the list. Changes go out in small, reversible pieces with the tracking already in place to tell whether they worked.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Confirm</strong>
        <span>Check the change against the baseline. Keep what earned its place, roll back what didn&rsquo;t, and move to the next item.</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

